nodecode-provenance is a rewrite of simin-yuan's simin-yuan/hermes-provenance-gate:
https://github.com/simin-yuan/hermes-provenance-gate
commit d8ded75deef198694639d8653c1834a26f3b0372
Apache-2.0 (LICENSE); the original's NOTICE reads: Copyright 2026 Simin (Simon) Yuan.

What was rewritten: the claim detector (patterns.lisp, from the original's
patterns.py), the sentence splitter and the verbatim quote matcher
(text.lisp, from claims.py and quotes.py), the pass/block decision and its
reasons (claims.lisp, from claims.py and verdict.py), and the surface the
user meets (cell.lisp): the two tools, the /provenance command, the manual
topic and the hook that gates a write. The English and Chinese verb tables,
the exemptions (questions, conditionals, negations, spec lines, generic
actors), the quote rules (verbatim match, shared content tokens, a quote
that drops a negation) and the evidence log were kept.

What was left out, and why: the original's own process hooks cannot exist
here, so Nodecode's one :tool point is hooked instead, and it reads the
text of an eval call that keeps a memory or a skill rather than a
memory/skill_manage tool call. The profile-wide search, the sender/role
attribution of each captured message, the "carried quote" rule for an edit
that keeps an existing quote, and the CLI's separate log/check/purge
subcommands were left out: the first needs a store the cell does not keep,
and the rest are a command's single sub-command here (report, check, purge).
The escape hatch is the same: observe mode records, block mode refuses.
